QuestGuidance.Register("en",443,{
[14145]="7000EC02\n1\tDefeat Morningthaw bears (total: 15)\tMorningthaw bears can be found around Tírith Rhaw in the Ettenmoors. Soldier Búzog asked you to defeat Morningthaw bears in the Ettenmoors.\n2\tTalk to Soldier Búzog\tSoldier Búzog is at Gramsfoot in the Ettenmoors. You should tell Soldier Búzog that the bears are no longer a hindrance to the construction of the barricades.\n",
[14146]="70044117\n1\tDisarm the Enemy's casks in the cisterns and defeat the Morgul forces Defeating the Morgul Captain will end this quest\tMorgul-orcs and goblins have snuck into the cisterns beneath Minas Tirith, hoping to destroy it from below while the forces of Gondor are occupied upon the wall.\n",
[14147]="7003FF7E\n1\tPreserve records (total: 4)\tThe records must be preserved if debts and ownership is to be known.\n",
[14148]="70066A48\n1\tUpokhir has asked you to deliver plans to his trusted confidants in Pahor Boha. Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.\t\n2\tTalk to Upokhir\tYou to have delivered plans to Upokhir's trusted confidants within Pahor Boha, and should report your success. Talk to Upokhir in Ost Arndír.\n",
[14149]="70042E89\n1\tSearch for Mírthel\tOst Sarram is located upon the southern cliffs in the western side of Southern Ithilien. You should search for Mírthel near Ost Sarram.\n2\tSpeak with Mírthel\tOst Sarram is located upon the southern cliffs in the western side of Southern Ithilien. You should talk to Mírthel near Ost Sarram.\n3\tDestroy Haradrim ladders (total: 6)\tOst Sarram is located upon the southern cliffs in the western side of Southern Ithilien. You should destroy Haradrim ladders upon the cliffs to stop the flow of men and supplies.\n4\tSpeak with Mírthel\tOst Sarram is located upon the southern cliffs in the western side of Southern Ithilien. You should speak to Mírthel near Ost Sarram.\n",
[14150]="70019D3C\n1\tPlace the vengeance arrow at the base of the lonely tree\tThe lonely tree where Núrelleth wants the vengeance arrow placed is on the bank of Anduin, east of Imlad Lalaith. Núrelleth wants the Elves of Lothlórien to remember her husband Faengris, and to that end, she would rather the vengeance arrow stand in his memory rather than be used to slay more Orcs.\n2\tTalk to Núrelleth at Telain Glorelloth\tNúrelleth is on Telain Glorelloth, on one of the flets that extends over the hedge that encircles Caras Galadhon. You have left the vengeance arrow at the lonely tree as Núrelleth requested of you and should now return to her.\n",
[14151]="70068ABF\n1\tWash your hands in the wash-basin\tRenowned head-cook Brûdo needs help catering a party for Umbar's elite. Start by washing your hands. A hand-washing basin can be found near Brûdo.\n2\tTalk to Brûdo\tNow that your hands are clean, speak to Brûdo to receive instructions. Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.\n3\tCarry the tray of food to table three\tNow that your hands are clean, pick up the first tray of food and take it to table three. The tray of food is on the table next to Brûdo.\n4\tTalk to Brûdo\tYou have made your first delivery. Speak to Brûdo to learn what to do next. Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.\n5\tClean up dirty dishes (total: 4)\tBrûdo told you to clean the dishes off tables four, five, six, and seven, near the dancing man. Brûdo still needs your help in the Upper Ward.\n6\tBring the dirty dishes to Brûdo\tYou have gathered the soiled plates. Bring them to Brûdo. Brûdo can be found in the bath-house of the Upper Ward.\n7\tDeliver the semolina cake to the guest\tBrûdo has asked you to deliver a special semolina cake to a guest. Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.\n8\tTalk to Brûdo\tYou have completed all your tasks and should speak to Brûdo. Brûdo can be found at the bath-house in the Upper Ward.\n",
[14152]="7002741D\n1\tDefeat Dragon-clan invaders (total: 12)\tDragon-clan invaders can be found all over the Herd-lands. You should defeat the Dragon-clan invaders as you wander throughout the farmlands.\n2\tReturn to Blodwen in the Herd-lands\tBlodwen can be found hiding among the rocks at the far southern edge of the Herd-lands in Trum Dreng. You should return to Blodwen and see if she has any more need of your assistance.\n",
[14153]="7004D370\n1\tDefeat Urdâr\tUrdâr can be found patrolling the Dale-lands. You have encountered the aggressive Urdâr. Roaming on the outskirts of the Dale-lands, the evil man patrols with his pets.\n2\tDefeat Urdâr\tUrdâr can be found patrolling the Dale-lands. You have encountered the aggressive Urdâr. Roaming on the outskirts of the Dale-lands, the evil man patrols with his pets.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Urdâr.\n",
[14154]="70043DAA\n1\tBring the supplies to Arthon quickly\tArthon is at the Armoury. You should bring the supplies to Arthon. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[14155]="70054F03\n1\tCollect rune-inscribed urns at Aufaltor\tRune-inscribed urns can be found at Aufaltor in Thuringwath.\n2\tCollect rune-inscribed urns at Aufaltor (total: 8)\tRune-inscribed urns can be found at Aufaltor in Thuringwath. You have discovered numerous urns bearing runic inscriptions in Aufaltor. You should collect a number of them for Mithrandir.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have collected many rune-inscribed urns at Aufaltor.\n",
[14156]="70054808\n1\tDestroy tents at Urshúlagar\tUrshúlagar can be found in Emyn Duir. You should destroy tents at Urshúlagar.\n2\tDestroy tents at Urshúlagar (total: 10)\tUrshúlagar can be found in Emyn Duir. You should destroy tents at Urshúlagar.\n3\tCompleted\tDestroyed many tents at Urshúlagar.\n",
[14157]="70054807\n1\tDefeat evil Men at Urshúlagar\tUrshúlagar can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat any evil Men you find at Urshúlagar.\n2\tDefeat Easterlings at Urshúlagar (total: 10)\030Defeat Black Númenóreans at Urshúlagar (total: 6)\tUrshúlagar can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat evil Men at Urshúlagar.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated many evil Men at Urshúlagar.\n",
[14158]="7001AB9A\n1\tCollect uruk-necklaces (total: 6)\tUruks may be found in Sâd-en-Dagor in Dol Guldur, north-east from Helethir. Stirnir has asked you to collect necklaces from the uruks in Dol Guldur.\n",
[14159]="7005025F\n1\tDefeat Jangovar in Utterby (total: 20)\030Defeat stubborn Jangovar lords (total: 3)\tMany Jangovar can be found inside Utterby. You should defeat Jangovar outside Utterby and inside Utterby: Continue the Fight.\n2\tTalk to Náin\tLord Náin can be found inside of the gates in Utterby. You should talk to Lord Náin.\n",
[14160]="70058F70\n1\tTalk to Wenda Cranesbill\tSpeak with Wenda to accept her kind offer.\n",
[14161]="700582F2\n1\tTalk to Wenda Cranesbill\tSpeak with Wenda to accept her kind offer.\n",
[14162]="700582F3\n1\tTalk to Wenda Cranesbill\tSpeak with Wenda to accept her kind offer.\n",
[14163]="7002672C\n1\tCollect the sceptre from the kergrim within Haudh Valandur\tHaudh Valandur is to the west of the Ranger-camp within the Way of Kings. Maladan asked you to venture within the tomb of Haudh Valandur and return a sceptre held by a kergrim within.\n2\tBring the sceptre to Maladan in the Way of Kings\tMaladan is at the Ranger-camp in the Way of Kings. Maladan will be eager to receive Valandur's sceptre.\n",
[14164]="700413C0\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the lumber camp (total: 5)\030Salvage tools from the lumber camp (total: 8)\030Find and speak with any survivors\tThe lumber camp is located east of Ethring in Ringló Vale. You should search the Lumber camp for any survivors and defeat any Orcs.\n2\tSpeak with Arvaethor\tSpeak with Arvaethor.\n",
[14165]="70054D07\n1\tTalk to Thurindol, Ereblen, and Tordoron\tThurindol, Ereblen, and Tordoron can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol, Ereblen, and Tordoron.\n2\tTalk to Thurindol\030Talk to Ereblen\030Talk to Tordoron\tThurindol, Ereblen, and Tordoron can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol, Ereblen, and Tordoron.\n3\tAttempt to enter Ghashan-kútot\tGhashan-kútot can be found in Minas Morgul. You should attempt to enter Ghashan-kútot.\n4\tFind someone who may be able to enter Ghashan-kútot\030Convince someone to get the book you seek\tSomeone who is able to enter Ghashan-kútot must be nearby. You should find someone who may be able to enter Ghashan-kútot.\n5\tSearch for the recently stolen book\tThe cataloguer's missing book is most likely still in Minas Morgul. You should search for the missing book, recently stolen from the Hall of Black Lore.\n6\tScattered pages of a book can be found blowing around in Minas Morgul. You should collect the pages.\t\n7\tBring the torn pages to the Black Númenórean cataloguer\tThe Black Númenórean cataloguer should still be near the Hall of Black Lore. You should bring the pages of the book to him for a trade.\n8\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[14166]="70054D14\n1\tEnter the Altar of Death\tThe Altar of Death can be found in the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul. You should enter the Altar of Death.\n2\tExamine the conflict around the altar\tThe Altar of Death can be found in the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul. You should examine the conflict around the altar.\n3\tExamine the altar\tThe Altar of Death can be found in the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul. You should examine the altar.\n4\tSeek out the rally points of the Morgul Vale (total: 5)\tRally points can be found throughout the Morgul Vale. You should seek out each rally point within the bounds of the Morgul Vale.\n5\tSeek out Thargaun at Ufurok\tThargaun can be found at Ufurok in Thuringwath. You should seek out Thargaun there.\n6\tDefeat foes at Ufurok (total: 8)\tUfurok can be found in Thuringwath. You should defeat foes at Ufurok so that your confrontation with Thargaun will be met with fewer surprises.\n7\tConfront Thargaun\tThargaun can be found at Ufurok in Thuringwath. You should confront Thargaun there.\n8\tTrap Thargaun with the stones of defeat!\tThargaun can be found at Ufurok in Thuringwath. You should trap Thargaun.\n9\tStop Thargaun's ritual\tThargaun's ritual can be found at Ufurok in Thuringwath. You should stop Thargaun's ritual.\n10\tDestroy the Orb of Death\tThe Orb of Death be found at Ufurok in Thuringwath. You should destroy the Orb of Death.\n11\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[14167]="70054D11\n1\tEnter the Altar of Despair\tThe Altar of Despair can be found in the Circle of Despair in Minas Morgul. You should enter the Altar of Despair.\n2\tExamine the barrier protecting the artifact\tThe Altar of Despair can be found in the Circle of Despair in Minas Morgul. You should examine the barrier protecting the artifact.\n3\tExamine the plaque\tThe Altar of Despair can be found in the Circle of Despair in Minas Morgul. You should examine the plaque next to the altar.\n4\tMake an etching of the plaque\tThe Altar of Despair can be found in the Circle of Despair in Minas Morgul. You should make an etching of the plaque.\n5\tTalk to Tordoron\tTordoron can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Tordoron.\n6\tSet the etching down on the map table\tThe map table can be found at Echad Uial. You should set the etching down on the map table.\n7\tExamine the etching and map\tThe map table can be found at Echad Uial. You should examine the etching and map.\n8\tTalk to Tordoron\tTordoron can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Tordoron.\n9\tThoroughly search all seven locations (total: 7)\tThe seven locations on the map can be found throughout Mordor. You should thoroughly search all seven.\n10\tReturn to the Altar of Despair\tThe Altar of Despair can be found in the Circle of Despair in Minas Morgul. You should return to the the Altar of Despair.\n11\tDestroy the Orb of Despair\tThe Altar of Despair can be found in the Circle of Despair in Minas Morgul. You should destroy the Orb of Despair.\n12\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[14168]="70054D12\n1\tTalk to Viznak at Barad Elenath\tViznak can be found at Barad Elenath. You should talk to Viznak.\n2\tWait for Viznak to return\tViznak can be found at Barad Elenath. You should wait for Viznak.\n3\tTalk to Viznak at Barad Elenath\tViznak can be found at Barad Elenath. You should talk to Viznak.\n4\tTravel to Agarnaith with Viznak\tViznak can be found in Agarnaith near Seregost. You should travel to Agarnaith and talk to Viznak.\n5\tTalk to Viznak in Agarnaith\tViznak can be found in Agarnaith near Seregost. You should talk to Viznak.\n6\tTalk to Viznak at his hideout\tViznak can be found in Agarnaith at his hideout. You should talk to Viznak.\n7\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[14169]="70054D13\n1\tDefeat shades and wights in Minas Morgul (total: 10)\tShades and wights can be found in Minas Morgul. You should defeat shades and wights in Minas Morgul.\n2\tFind and defeat Thargaun\tThargaun must be somewhere in Minas Morgul. You should seek out Thargaun to learn more about the second artifact.\n3\tTalk to Thargaun\tThargaun is in Minas Morgul. You should talk to Thargaun.\n4\tSearch a location where the artifact might be\030Search a second location where the artifact might be\030Search a third location where the artifact might be\tThe artifact you seek is somewhere in Cirith Ungol. You should search some locations where the artifact might be.\n5\tSearch one more location where the artifact might be\tThe artifact you seek is somewhere in Cirith Ungol. You should search one more location where the artifact might be.\n6\tExamine the pile of dust\tThe strange pile of dust can be found in Cirith Ungol. You should examine the pile of dust.\n7\tFollow the scratch marks into Torech Ungol\tThe scratch marks lead into Torech Ungol. You should follow the scratch marks.\n8\tFind the artifact you seek\030Examine the bones for any sign of the artifact\tThe artifact you seek can be found in Torech Ungol. You should find the artifact.\n9\tDestroy the Orb of Sorrow\tThe Orb of Sorrow can be found in Torech Ungol. You should destroy the Orb of Sorrow.\n10\tResist the vision of sorrow\tThe Orb of Sorrow can be found in Torech Ungol. Try to resist the visions of sorrow.\n11\tResist the vision of sorrow\tThe Orb of Sorrow can be found in Torech Ungol. Try to resist the visions of sorrow.\n12\tResist the vision of sorrow\tThe Orb of Sorrow can be found in Torech Ungol. Try to resist the visions of sorrow.\n13\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[14170]="70054D15\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Minas Morgul (total: 8)\tOrcs can be found upon the Circle of Wrath in Minas Morgul. You should defeat Orcs in Minas Morgul.\n2\tInjured Orcs can be found upon the Circle of Wrath in Minas Morgul. You should question those Orcs that you have injured.\t\n3\tTrack the group of the Orcs who make for Nurn\tA group of Orcs found the artifact you seek and left the city. You should track the group of Orcs as they make their way towards Nurn.\n4\tTalk to the injured Orc\tThe injured Orc can be found in Talath Úrui. You should find out what happened to this group of Orcs.\n5\tTalk to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found at Echad Uial. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[14171]="7005520C\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Wilderfolk of the Vales of Anduin.\n",
[14172]="70055206\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Wilderfolk of the Vales of Anduin.\n",
[14173]="70055207\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Wilderfolk of the Vales of Anduin.\n",
[14174]="70055208\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred to the Wilderfolk of the Vales of Anduin.\n",
[14175]="70054836\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive a Vales of Anduin barter currency allowance.\n",
[14176]="7000702C\n1\tDefeat cold-worms (total: 10)\tWorms can be found in the western pass of Ram Dúath, north of Esteldín. Melthindir has asked you to clear the worms from the western pass of Ram Dúath, making it safe to bring a force through the pass into Angmar.\n2\tReturn to Melthindir\tMelthindir awaits your return at Esteldín. You made your way into the valley and slew the worms you found there. You should return to Melthindir with news of your victory.\n",
})
